WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
Let you opponents tremble with fear

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.570
I’ll stop him!

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.790
Alright, he fell for it.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.880
That's disappointing, Miku...I’ve already warned you.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.180
Shiro!

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.890
Hit it towards me.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.770
I can get it!

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.440
What? I didn’t touch him!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.280
Yellow?

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.990
Was there even contact?

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.490
Who knows.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.960
But the opponent baited him.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.960
He's a sly one...

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.640
Damn, we conceded.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.070
The current score is 1-1.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.740
ETU’s pulling out all the stops, aren’t they?

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:09.040
Still, I think Tokyo Victory will dominate from here on out.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.710
The difference in their strengths is too wide.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.340
That reporter’s pissing me off.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.970
But still, I wonder whether they'll be alright...

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.570
I-I’m sorry!

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.030
It was my foul that...

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.330
It's not your fault, so don’t worry about it.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.960
That’s right, moron!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.290
That bastard Mochida plays dirty!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.300
He once tricked the referee into giving me a card too...

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.340
Don't boast about it.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:06.140
Still, if we don’t come up with a plan for the second half, we’re not going to win the midfield.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.720
Exactly.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.020
Because of that, it's time for a tactical change: Miyano in, Ishigami out.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:17.150
In the second half, we'll switch formation from 4-5-1 to 3-6-1.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.490
The attacking Miyano will be used to seize the midfield.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.820
Gino and Akasaki will play up front.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.820
Do get along.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.330
Take care of me, Zaki.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.330
I'm exhausted from taking on two defenders just now.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.500
Go forward, Miyano.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.380
Don’t worry about tracking back.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:38.710
Yes!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:45.220
Whether or not the opponents exploit the space left behind by Miyano will depend on the two of you.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.720
So go all out, you guys!

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.390
For the second half, the opponents will be full of themselves after that equalizer.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.650
Don’t panic even if they're dominating.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.320
So long as that look on your faces don’t die,

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.980
We have a chance to win this!

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.660
Beat those guys with a shitty name like “Victory”.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.740
Straight down to the ground!

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:15.330
All right, let’s roll guys! Let's destroy Victory!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.550
At moments like these, Kuroda’s really useful.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.260
Tsubaki.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.220
If you falter now, your efforts in the first half will count for nothing.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.190
Don't be afraid to commit fouls.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:41.730
Conversely, make the crowd tremble with fear.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.570
Yes.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:15.390
So they sacrificed a defender for a midfielder, eh?

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.270
Tatsumi...

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.730
Are you planning a midfield battle?

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:28.490
Sorry though. We, Tokyo Victory, will never lose in a direct confrontation against small teams.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.380
So you’re still coming after me, even after you got a card, eh?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.220
Charge!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.560
All right! Go for it!

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.950
Just what is the offense thinking?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.000
Attack!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:22.080
Pass it!

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.170
So close!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.090
The left side’s unguarded! Attack!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.140
That's space left behind by Miyano!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.220
A chance!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.100
Charge!

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:39.850
Nice cover!

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:44.860
As expected of Murakoshi. He's good.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.110
Amazing.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.280
That was such a quick wing play.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.910
Murakoshi’s amazing.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:56.950
Now, my turn...

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.160
Miyano, just keep on charging!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.630
Akasaki, remember to assist him!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.550
Zaki!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.260
Tamba, it's yours!

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.140
Nice link-up play.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.350
Be careful!

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.610
Get another man down the left wing!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.030
Hey, over here!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:34.950
Mochida!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.080
Nice one, Tsubaki!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.540
Bastard...

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.420
We're fending them off!

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:50.500
Dad...

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:58.600
I've...never found ETU's play...

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.220
...to be that interesting.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.820
Only fifteen minutes left in the second half.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:20.870
Tatsumi…

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.540
He’s going to use up all three substitutes that early?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:30.210
Well, Sera and Tamba have been running around throughout the match.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:38.010
Is that okay, Tatsumi? The match is now out of your control.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.810
It’ll be okay.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.270
Now to see how things will go.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.060
M-Manager?!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:51.190
Didn’t I say before the match?

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.730
My goal is to draw at best.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:55.110
But…

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.160
I hate speculating on psychology...

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:03.410
Now that we're late into the game, the deciding factor now will be their willpower.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:09.080
From what I saw at the camp, they all wanted to win badly.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:17.420
What matters now is whether they will be able to play better than the champions.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.300
In order to transform this team,

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.260
The key here...

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:28.520
...is to truly understand their capabilities.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.820
It's been awhile since we started the second half.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.570
The opponents should be tiring out.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.080
As substitutes, we should be running at them to create chances.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:46.910
Akasaki!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.500
It's our turn to seize the initiative. Just you wait and see!

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:57.260
What?!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.260
The international, Shironishi!

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.680
He's still able to run?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.770
So we're attacking once again...

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.940
That lazy bastard.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:22.950
Gino has the cheek to stroll through the game?

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.830
But I was constantly double-teamed during the first half.

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.410
That's quite enough for the day.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.330
Tsubaki! Chase him down!

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.080
This is it!

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.930
Hey! That was a close one!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:55.480
Darn, why does that Brazilian have to flop at the most crucial of times?

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.610
It seems like I will have to score myself.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.410
That is your strength, Tsubaki.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:11.960
Do your best.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.670
No matter times you fail...

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:19.210
All you need is that one chance to dazzle the crowd and frighten your opponents.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:24.430
Bring out the spirit of Giant Killing in you.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.560
I won't let you have your way!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.740
Ten minutes left in the second half...

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.950
A draw should be a fairly good result against such an opponent.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.410
How could you be satisfied with just a draw?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.880
Anyway, the lads are doing a good job.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:02.260
Though we don't seem to have control of the match...can we score another goal?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.640
Well, I hope so but...

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.430
The control of the ball...

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.890
The opponent's teamwork...

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.480
The determination of the internationals...

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:19.520
As well as the deafening cheers of their supporters...

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:35.210
To win with these factors against us is certainly not an easy task...

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.920
Their passes are quick!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:44.800
They went past Tsubaki!

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.590
Damn it!

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:52.100
Sugi, mark Leornado! Kuroda, prevent Mochida from shooting!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:57.810
He's through!

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.190
I'll stop him!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:02.400
I will...

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.490
Was it too tame?

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.620
Dori, save it!

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.410
Your hard work has gone to waste.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.370
Thank you, Tsubaki!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.370
We conceded...and it's all my fault.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:11.140
Get up, Tsubaki. Today's mistakes weren't your fault.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.600
That look on his face...this match's over for Tsubaki.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:26.320
Sigh, and we were holding them up for so long...

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.780
What are you doing, manager?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.950
Observing the players.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:35.370
Huh?

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.910
Only five minutes left...

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:45.960
We had played on level terms with the champs but eventually handed them the lead...

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:49.380
In such a situation, what state of mind will the players have?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.550
Have they cracked?

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.640
Or otherwise.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.100
We can clearly see each player's personality from this.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.850
Those who think that all is lost now...

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.020
The footballing gods won't be smiling upon them.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.110
Tsubaki!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:11.860
Don't get your head down!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.950
Or you'll be taken advantage of!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:15.320
Yes...

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:18.040
Damn it.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.330
We'll be in trouble if Tsubaki is targeted.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.460
That said though, I'll be leaving a hole if I were to assist him.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.550
Should Akasaki track back?

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.220
But that will reduce the number of people in attack.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:38.390
The team's balance and tactics shouldn't be in your area of responsibility.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.940
That's why I stripped you of your captaincy.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.530
Stop wasting time!

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.240
What are you guys doing?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:01.120
That's the natural thing to do when you're leading.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.710
I've always been playing for the sake of the team.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:13.630
The captain's armband served as a constant reminder of that to me.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.890
What should I do now that I have lost it?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:23.310
How do you see me as player?

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.810
There's space behind them!

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:29.730
Crap, a counter-attack!

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:39.870
From here on, seek something in yourself that will help you to succeed.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.250
Don't let him pass, Murakoshi!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.420
What should I do?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.670
The present me...

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.680
What can I do?!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.470
Great defending! As expected of Murakoshi!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.560
That's our Mr ETU!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.730
Murakoshi's not gonna lose out!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:15.360
This is not the time to think about losing!

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:20.570
You won't win like this, Murakoshi!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.760
Go on, Murakoshi!

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:41.510
I'll take on No.10!

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.390
A one-two pass!

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:47.890
Come on, Murakoshi!

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:50.900
Position yourselves!

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:52.650
Where will it come from?

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.280
Shoot, Murakoshi!

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:56.800
Manager...

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.880
Sorry for calling you out!

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:06.640
Give me a break. Calling me out in a place like this.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.810
What's so bad about it? It's near too.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.860
This is a nice amusement park.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.440
It makes you feel like being at home.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:21.530
Amazing, isn't it?

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:27.370
Although they're the same rides like the ones in the city, they're all different in style and color.

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.330
Just like how it is with clubs and teams.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.750
They each have their own colors.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:36.670
While ETU's color-

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:41.800
What do you know about them...as someone who once abandoned the team?

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.340
Are you done?

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.140
It's only a draw.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.850
And the opponents weren't even playing seriously.

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.350
Our problems were exposed one after another.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.810
With that attitude of yours,

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.650
We'll get a proper beating the next time round!

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:07.870
How long more are you going to be deluded, Mr ETU?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.000
You slow-moving lump of meat.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.080
How many times am I going to say it?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.710
I don't need a captain like that!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.550
Don't you understand?

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:22.960
You bastard...

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:25.260
You did take that shot and scored though...

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:30.890
But you were charging through blindly after that, right?

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.690
I want you to etch that memory deeply into your mind.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.950
The cheers of hundreds of our fans...

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:53.500
The childish and thrilled expressions on your teammates...

00:21:56.370 --> 00:22:01.590
Your meaning to the team all this while...all of it were summed up in that single moment.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.590
The team's color...

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:08.720
It's you, Murakoshi.

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:12.310
Keep looking forward!

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:18.100
The condition for this is...

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:24.480
Abiding to my absolute command, fully understanding my actions and relaying them to others.

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:27.740
Report everything you notice to me.

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:30.530
Ignore what others think of you.

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:34.740
And above all else, continue developing as a player.

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:37.040
I will not hold back if you break any of these conditions.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:38.830
One more thing,

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:43.590
Even if you are going to kill me, do it after I get sacked.

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:50.720
Then you really have to be careful not to get the boot.

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:16.970
Mixing it up?

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:18.470
Get yourself prepared, quick!

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:20.020
We're heading off!

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:21.350
The next person here is...

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:25.230
No matter how outstanding the manager and his players are...

00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:26.520
Who are you?

00:24:26.610 --> 00:24:27.400
You have the luck!
